,"children":[["$","$L5",null,{"children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":["I'm ","Taiwo Adebola",", a cybersecurity student and aspiring software engineer based in ","Nigeria",". The honest summary of what I do: I build things to understand them."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["That habit started with small scripts and utilities and grew into the collection you can see in"," ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/projects","className":"text-accent-blue underline-offset-4 hover:underline","children":"my projects"}]," ","— a church service planner with a live document preview, a Telegram bot with memory, a fintech prototype built around a proper ledger, and a self-hosted deployment environment I operate and troubleshoot myself. None of it is decorative. Each project exists because I wanted to know how that kind of system actually works, and building it was the only honest way to find out."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The thread connecting it all is a pull toward the layer beneath the layer — what the browser actually sends, what the proxy actually does with it, what the database actually records. My study of cybersecurity sharpened that instinct into a discipline: understand the system before you trust it, and describe the system accurately before you claim anything about it."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"I distinguish carefully between what I've built and what I'm becoming. I'm not yet a professional engineer with years of production experience — I'm a serious student of the craft with a growing portfolio of real, working projects and the discipline to label them accurately. What I can offer today is genuine curiosity, honest engineering, and the habit of finishing what I start."}]]}]}],["$","$L5",null,{"delay":0.1,"children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","aside",null,{"aria-label":"Current focus","className":"rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-6